  ====
  - [[Page~167 箇(3)個(3)个(3)]]
    ==
    - The first of these is a bamboo stalk; <# TODO $箇go3 #>
    - a classifier applied to human beings,
      to inanimate things, particularly of a roundish or compact form,
      periods of time, coins, schemes, plats of land, &c.,
      more widely than any other;
    - denotes objects when spoken of individually;
    - an individual or thing, as in the phrases
      _~~ch(e/)(3)~~ ``(2)ch(e/)`` ko(3)_ [[ze2 go3]]
        or
      _(1)n(i/) ko(3)_ [[ni1 go3]]
        this one;
    - _~~(2)n(a/)~~ ``(5)n(a/)`` ko(3)_ [[naa5 go3]]
        or
      _ko(3) ko(3)_ [[go3 go3]] <# TODO: modernise to $嗰go2 #>
      (often pronounced _(2)ko ko(3)_ [[go2 go3]],
      to distinguish it from _ko(3) ko(3)_ [[go3 go3]] every)
        that one;
    - a pronoun, this, this one, but need not always be translated;
    - stands for the possessive case,
      as _(5)ngo ko(3) (4)t(')au_ [[ngo5 go3 tau4]],
        my head;
    - when following the negative _mok(9)_ [[mok6]] or _(5)mai_ [[mai5]],
      specifies the following noun;
    - as _mok(9) ko(3) h(u:)(3)_
        [[mok6 go3 heoi3]]
        don't go, _i.e._ don't [do] that going;
    - _(5)mai ko(3) (2)hai ch(')(u:)(3)_
        [[mai5 go3 hai2 cyu3]]
        don't stand there;
    - _ko(3) ko(3) (1)t(o\) (5)yau_
        [[go3 go3 dou1 jau5]],
        every body has it, we have all things;
    - _sai(3) ko(3)_
        [[sai3 go3]]
        the little thing, the darling, the pet;
    - _~~ko(3)~~ ``(2)ko`` tik(7)_ [[go2 dik1]]
      is used with less speciality than _~~ko(3)~~ ``(2)ko`` ko(3)_ [[go2 go3]],
      as _~~ko(3)~~ ``(2)ko`` tik(7) hai(6) mat(7) (4)yan ``k(e/)(3)``_
        [[go2 dik1 hai6 mat1 jan4 ge3]],
        whose is that?
    - _mat(7) (5)y(e/) w(a/)(6) ko(3) (4)'m hai(6)_
        [[mat1 je5 waa6 go3 m4 hai6]]
        who says it is not so?
    - _(5)m(o\) ko(3) (4)'m (1)nau_
        [[mou5 go3 m4 nau1]],
        who is not angry?
    - _tai(6) (i/)(6) ko(3)_
        [[dai6 ji6 go3]]
        another;
    - _(2)k(i/) ko(3) (1)s(e/)ung_
        [[gei2 go3 soeng1]],
        several boxes;
    - _(4)'m (1)fan tak(7) ko(3) sh(o\)(3)_
        [[m4 fan1 dak1 go3 sou3]]
